# ComposeServer Plugin Loader — config-manifest discovery, validated-before-instantiation; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-CS-LOADER]

> The loader turns the hand-wired plugin library ([SPEC:CXC-COMPOSESERVER]'s `standup()`/`ComposeServer`, which take HAND-INSTANTIATED plugin objects) into an actual host: a per-tenant manifest declares which plugins to load; the loader resolves each plugin's CLASS, validates its declared `config:` against that plugin's own pydantic `Config` model BEFORE instantiating it, and hands the resulting instances to the EXISTING `standup()`/`ComposeServer.add_tenant()` unchanged. An invalid config or an unmet `requires:` floor PARKS the plugin loudly, naming the specific offending item; nothing crashes the loader or a sibling plugin. This is a build spec — every MUST below carries a machine-checkable acceptance criterion and, where the failure class needs eyes, a `verify.human` gate.

---

