**Version**: 0.1 — 2026-08-24, initial build spec, authored from the composeio-hardware-architect's dispatch specifying the plugin loader's design intent (config-manifest discovery, config validation before instantiation, requires-floor/subprocess-pending reuse, per-tenant strictness, status-surface extension) as MUST/SHOULD predicates with verify.machine/verify.human acceptance tiers, per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE].
**Status**: Draft — awaiting architect/David ratify. Three open forks: [DD-CSL-DISCOVERY] (config-manifest vs. entry_points auto-discovery), [DD-CSL-MANIFEST-FORMAT] (file format + per-tenant location), [DD-CSL-HOT-RELOAD] (manifest hot-reload in v1, architect leans OUT). The `david-ruling`-tagged nodes ([CXC-CSL-REQUIRES-FLOOR], [CXC-CSL-CONTINUOUS-REBIND], [CXC-CSL-SUBPROCESS-PENDING], [CXC-CSL-PER-TENANT]) carry David's word by inheritance from their cited source nodes, not as new rulings of their own.
